<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Drama, Narrative-driven.</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> As other narrative-driven SCPs, the page will have different iterations of the SCP article.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A gladius that can transform into a ballet dancing woman-like fighting automaton. It has always a host which, when killed, pass the &quot;hosting&quot; to their murder. If the owner was killed in an unintentional way or to a non-humanoid killer, the SCP will become the protector of its host until it is defeated. SCP is looking to be a &quot;Perfect Weapon&quot; for a &quot;Perfect Warrior&quot;, so it will defend its host from killing attempts turning into its automaton form. Also it will keep and share every past hosts' memories, especially skills that can be used on warfare, turning the actual host more proficient as a combatant. This is connected to the SCP “ballerina&quot; fighting style as one of its past owners was a ballet dancer that fought Russian Civil War.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The narrative is more centred on the hosts, the &quot;SCP-XXXX-A&quot;. There will be three hosts:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>First Host:</strong> They'll be an unintentional host as they defeated the SCP while retrieving it. This host will discover SCP “memory flash drive&quot; powers and will be turned into the subject of an mnestic experiment to discover the SCP memories. As they are experimented, they start presenting PTSD signals by living another person's memories (mainly killings and war memories). As they kill another agent during an hyperarousal episode, Foundation changes SCP host.</li>
<li><strong>Second Host:</strong> With the second, researchers try to identify why the sword changes forms. While doing it, they determine that SCP protects its owner when they're off guard. The host accepts to take part in a test where it is surprised by non-lethal attacks every now and then. Host becomes paranoid because of it and presents homicidal behavior. Foundation changes the host again.</li>
<li><strong>Third Host:</strong> Losing two agents for the SCP, the Foundation decides that the third have to be protected at all costs. Psychological, therapeutic and psychiatric treatments are offered to it and a Special Task Force protects it everytime. Anyway, the STF commander is tasked to kill the third host and become the fourth if anything out of the ordinary occurs.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Most of the time, the hosts actions are more connected to the Foundation's experiments and protocols than the SCP itself:</p>
<ul>
<li>The first host develops PTSD because of the mnestics.</li>
<li>The second host becomes paranoid because of the ambush experiment.</li>
<li>The last owner is treated as an object, being constantly protected and losing his free will.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I want to know if you think the SCP is weak for being focused on its &quot;owners''. Also, I want to know if the narratives are interesting or if in its anachronic file-based narrative the story will become boring. I'll try to keep with the &quot;Cold, not Cruel&quot; and &quot;Flawed, not Fools&quot; all the time, but I need more critics about it.</p>

